# The open data of the City and County of Denver on ArcGIS Online: the off-leash dog parks, the
# animal cases of the 311 service requests, and the kennel licenses. The fields and types are
# written by hand over the ArcGIS REST query operation of each layer and table.

extend type Query {
	"""
	The off-leash dog parks of the City and County of Denver, sorted by name, with whether each one is fenced, has
	shade and has drinking water, its size, the year it was built and its condition. Denver has 18 of them. These
	are city dog parks in Denver, Colorado. The national parks and their trails are in the nps fields. To find the
	parks nearest to a clinic owner, select nearestDogParks on the owner. One query to Denver's open data.
	"""
	denverDogParks(
		"Only the parks that are fenced (true) or open (false). Leave it out for every park. All 18 parks are fenced."
		fenced: Boolean
		"Only the parks with shade (true) or without (false). Both leave out the parks without a recorded value."
		shade: Boolean
		"""
		Only the parks with drinking water for dogs (true) or without (false). Both leave out the parks without a
		recorded value.
		"""
		water: Boolean
	): [DenverDogPark!]!

	"""
	Animal cases that people reported to Denver 311, the city's service line, such as barking dogs, loose animals,
	strays, lost pets, animal bites and injured wildlife, the most recent first, one page at a time. The table
	holds the cases of the last 12 months, about 10,800 animal cases. About four in five come without an address
	or coordinates, and most of those were closed as Closed - Answer Provided.
	To count cases by type, use denverAnimalServiceRequestCounts. To count cases without reading them, select only
	totalRequests. Selecting totalPages or totalRequests costs a second query.
	"""
	denverAnimalServiceRequests(
		"Only cases of these types, for example [BARKING_DOG, LOOSE_ANIMAL]. Leave it out for every animal case."
		caseTypes: [DenverAnimalCaseType!]
		"Only cases at an incident address in this five-digit ZIP code, for example 80204. It also matches a ZIP+4 code."
		zipCode: String
		"Only cases in this Denver city council district, from 1 to 11."
		councilDistrict: Int
		"Only cases created on this day or later, for example 2026-09-01."
		createdFrom: Date
		"Only cases created on this day or earlier, for example 2026-09-30."
		createdTo: Date
		"The page to return, starting at 1. A value below 1 returns the first page."
		page: Int! = 1
		"The number of cases on a page, from 1 to 50. A value outside that range is moved to the nearest limit."
		size: Int! = 10
	): DenverAnimalServiceRequestPage!

	"""
	The number of animal cases that people reported to Denver 311, by type of case, the largest count first, for
	example how many barking dog complaints Denver had in a month. Types without a case are left out. The table
	holds the cases of the last 12 months. One query to Denver's open data.
	"""
	denverAnimalServiceRequestCounts(
		"Only cases created on this day or later, for example 2026-09-01."
		createdFrom: Date
		"Only cases created on this day or earlier, for example 2026-09-30."
		createdTo: Date
		"Only cases at an incident address in this five-digit ZIP code, for example 80204. It also matches a ZIP+4 code."
		zipCode: String
		"Only cases in this Denver city council district, from 1 to 11."
		councilDistrict: Int
	): [DenverAnimalCaseCount!]!

	"""
	Where to board a dog or cat in Denver: the dog boarding, doggie daycare, grooming and training businesses, pet
	stores, shelters and animal hospitals that hold an active kennel license from the City and County of Denver,
	sorted by name, one page at a time, such as Daily Wag Doggie Daycare, Woof Resorts, Grand Central Grooming, Pavlov
	Dog Training, Petco, the Dumb Friends League shelter and Tender Touch Animal Hospital. Denver has about 70 of
	them. One query to Denver's open data.
	"""
	denverKennelLicenses(
		"""
		Text that the business name, the trade name or the address contains, in upper or lower case, for example
		animal hospital or Kalamath. Leave it out for every license.
		"""
		search: String = ""
		"The page to return, starting at 1. A value below 1 returns the first page."
		page: Int! = 1
		"The number of licenses on a page, from 1 to 50. A value outside that range is moved to the nearest limit."
		size: Int! = 10
	): DenverKennelLicensePage!
}

extend type Owner {
	"""
	The off-leash dog parks of the City and County of Denver nearest to the owner's address, nearest first, within
	5 km, with the distance to the centre of each park. The US Census geocoder finds the address and Denver's dog
	park layer lists the parks around it. The list is empty for an owner who lives outside Denver, without a call,
	and when the geocoder cannot find the address. It is null when a service cannot be reached.
	"""
	nearestDogParks(
		"How many parks to return, from 1 to 10."
		first: Int! = 3
	): [DenverDogPark!]
}

"""
An off-leash dog park of the City and County of Denver, Colorado. The city records whether it is fenced, has shade
and has water as yes or no, and leaves some of them empty.
"""
type DenverDogPark {
	"The city's identifier of the park in its dog park layer."
	id: ID!
	"The name of the park, for example Railyard Dog Park."
	name: String!
	"The city's code for the park location, for example 922."
	locationCode: String
	"Whether the park is fenced. Null when the city has not recorded it."
	fenced: Boolean
	"Whether the park has shade. Null when the city has not recorded it."
	shade: Boolean
	"Whether the park has drinking water. Null when the city has not recorded it."
	water: Boolean
	"The size of the park in acres, for example 0.57."
	acres: Float
	"The year the dog park was built, for example 2010."
	yearBuilt: Int
	"""
	The condition of the park as the city assessed it. The city writes it as a word, such as Good or Excellent, or
	as a score out of 100, such as 80, and the text is passed on as the city wrote it.
	"""
	condition: String
	"The day of the assessment that the condition comes from."
	conditionAssessedDate: Date
	"The latitude of the centre of the park, in degrees."
	latitude: Float
	"The longitude of the centre of the park, in degrees."
	longitude: Float
	"""
	The distance from the owner's address to the centre of the park, in metres. Null in denverDogParks, which lists
	the parks without an address.
	"""
	distanceInMetres: Int
}

"""
One page of Denver 311 animal cases. The cases are sorted by the day they were created, the most recent first.
"""
type DenverAnimalServiceRequestPage {
	"The cases on this page."
	requests: [DenverAnimalServiceRequest!]!
	"The page that was returned, starting at 1."
	page: Int!
	"The number of pages available for the same filters and size."
	totalPages: Int!
	"The number of cases that match the filters, counted across every page."
	totalRequests: Int!
}

"""
An animal case that someone reported to Denver 311, the city's service line, by phone, in the PocketGov app or by
email. Denver leaves the neighbourhood, division, type and topic of these cases empty, so the case type is their
only classification, and about four in five cases come without an address or coordinates.
"""
type DenverAnimalServiceRequest {
	"The identifier of the case in the 311 table."
	id: ID!
	"The type of case."
	caseType: DenverAnimalCaseType
	"The case summary as 311 wrote it, for example Barking Dog."
	summary: String!
	"How far the case got, for example New, Closed - Answer Provided or Closed - Transferred to External Agency."
	status: String
	"How the case reached 311, for example Phone, PocketGov or Email - 311."
	source: String
	"The day the case was created."
	createdDate: Date
	"The time the case was created, in Denver's local time and the US format 311 uses, for example 9/30/2026 11:42:51 AM."
	createdAt: String
	"The day the case was closed, or null while it is open."
	closedDate: Date
	"The time the case was closed, in the same format as createdAt."
	closedAt: String
	"The city agency the case was filed under, for example Public Health & Environment or Safety."
	agency: String
	"The address of the incident, for example 511 N Lowell Blvd. Null for most cases."
	address: String
	"The intersection of the incident, as two streets joined with and, for a case reported at a corner."
	intersection: String
	"The ZIP code of the incident, with five digits or as a ZIP+4 code, for example 80219 or 80239-4053."
	zipCode: String
	"The Denver city council district of the incident, from 1 to 11."
	councilDistrict: Int
	"The Denver police district of the incident."
	policeDistrict: Int
	"The latitude of the incident, in degrees. Null for most cases."
	latitude: Float
	"The longitude of the incident, in degrees. Null for most cases."
	longitude: Float
}

"The number of Denver 311 animal cases of one type."
type DenverAnimalCaseCount {
	"The type of case."
	caseType: DenverAnimalCaseType!
	"The number of cases."
	cases: Int!
}

"The types of animal case in Denver's 311 service requests. Each one stands for one case summary that 311 uses."
enum DenverAnimalCaseType {
	"A question about adopting an animal or about an animal on hold. Filed as Animal Adoption/Hold Inquiry."
	ADOPTION_OR_HOLD_INQUIRY
	"Someone lost a pet. Filed as Lost my Pet."
	LOST_PET
	"A complaint about a barking dog. Filed as Barking Dog."
	BARKING_DOG
	"Someone wants to give up a pet. Filed as Pet Surrender."
	PET_SURRENDER
	"An animal running loose. Filed as Loose Animal."
	LOOSE_ANIMAL
	"A dog off its leash with its owner nearby. Filed as Loose Dog (With owner)."
	LOOSE_DOG_WITH_OWNER
	"Someone is holding a stray animal they found. Filed as Holding Stray Animal."
	HOLDING_STRAY_ANIMAL
	"A call passed to Denver Animal Protection. Filed as Denver Animal Protection 720-913-2080."
	ANIMAL_PROTECTION_CALL
	"A wild animal that is hurt. Filed as Injured Wildlife."
	INJURED_WILDLIFE
	"A question or complaint about a wild animal. Filed as Wildlife."
	WILDLIFE
	"An owner wants to pick up a pet from the shelter. Filed as Pet Redemption."
	PET_REDEMPTION
	"Animal droppings left behind. Filed as Animal Excrement."
	ANIMAL_EXCREMENT
	"A question about a pet license or a microchip. Filed as Pet License/Micro Chip."
	PET_LICENSE_OR_MICROCHIP
	"A dangerous or aggressive animal that has not bitten anyone. Filed as Dangerous/Aggressive (Not a Bite)."
	DANGEROUS_OR_AGGRESSIVE_ANIMAL
	"A case about a business that makes pet food. Filed as Pet Food Manufacturing."
	PET_FOOD_MANUFACTURING
	"A pet or another domestic animal that is hurt. Filed as Injured Domestic Animal."
	INJURED_DOMESTIC_ANIMAL
	"A dead animal to be removed. Filed as Dead Animal."
	DEAD_ANIMAL
	"A bite or attack that broke the skin. Filed as Bite/Attack (Broken the skin)."
	BITE_OR_ATTACK
	"Filed as Animal Bite (non human)."
	ANIMAL_BITE_NON_HUMAN
	"A case about a city dog park. Filed as Dog Parks."
	DOG_PARK
	"Too many animals kept at one place. Filed as Too many animals."
	TOO_MANY_ANIMALS
	"A case about breeding animals or service animals. Filed as Breeding Animals / Service Animals."
	BREEDING_OR_SERVICE_ANIMALS
	"An animal left in a vehicle. Filed as Animal in Vehicle."
	ANIMAL_IN_VEHICLE
	"A complaint about an animal presented as a service animal. Filed as Non-Service Animal Complaint."
	NON_SERVICE_ANIMAL_COMPLAINT
	"Another complaint about an animal. Filed as Animal Complaint."
	ANIMAL_COMPLAINT
}

"""
One page of Denver kennel licenses. The licenses are sorted by the name of the business.
"""
type DenverKennelLicensePage {
	"The licenses on this page."
	licenses: [DenverKennelLicense!]!
	"The page that was returned, starting at 1."
	page: Int!
	"The number of pages available for the same search and size."
	totalPages: Int!
	"The number of licenses that match the search, counted across every page."
	totalLicenses: Int!
}

"""
An active kennel license that the City and County of Denver issued to a business, such as a doggie day care, a
groomer, a pet store, an animal shelter or an animal hospital.
"""
type DenverKennelLicense {
	"The city's business file number of the license, for example 2001-BFN-63777."
	licenseNumber: String!
	"The legal name of the business, for example TENDER TOUCH ANIMAL HOSPITAL."
	entityName: String
	"The name the business trades under, for example TENDER TOUCH. Denver leaves it empty for some businesses."
	tradeName: String
	"The status of the license, for example License Issued - Active."
	status: String
	"The day the license expires."
	expirationDate: Date
	"The address of the business, for example 350 KALAMATH ST."
	address: String
	"The five-digit ZIP code of the business."
	zipCode: String
	"""
	The latitude of the business in degrees, converted from the State Plane coordinates Denver stores. Null for a
	license without a position.
	"""
	latitude: Float
	"The longitude of the business in degrees, converted in the same way. Null for a license without a position."
	longitude: Float
}
